<!-- title: The pitch deck: an agentic team, from the Algarve -->
<!-- summary: The pitch for investors in slides: the problem, what we do, the proof, how we make money, the go-to-market, open source, the team, the company and what the investment is for. No numbers and no projections, on purpose. -->
<style>
.deck{--paper:var(--surface);font-size:17px}.deck *{box-sizing:border-box}
.deck .slide{position:relative;aspect-ratio:16/9;background:var(--paper);border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:16px;box-shadow:var(--shadow);padding:2.2em 2.6em;margin:0 0 1.6em;overflow:hidden;display:flex;flex-direction:column}
.deck .slide h1{font:800 3.2em/1.05 Georgia,serif;margin:.3em 0}.deck .slide h2{font:700 1.7em/1.2 Georgia,serif;margin:0 0 .8em;border:0;padding:0}
.deck .slide-n{position:absolute;right:1em;bottom:.6em;font:600 .75em ui-monospace,monospace;color:var(--ink-2)}
.deck .kick{font:700 .8em ui-monospace,monospace;letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--accent);margin:0}.deck .big{font-size:1.25em}
.deck .cover{display:flex;flex-direction:column;justify-content:center;height:100%}
.deck .cap{color:var(--ink-2);font-size:.85em;margin:auto 0 0}.deck ul,.deck ol{margin:.4em 0 0;padding-left:1.2em}.deck li{margin:.35em 0}
.deck .cols{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(var(--n,3),1fr);gap:1em;margin:.4em 0}
.deck .box{border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:12px;padding:.8em 1em;background:var(--surface-2);font-size:.9em}.deck .box b{display:block;font-size:1.1em;margin-bottom:.3em}
.deck .box.hi{border:2px solid var(--accent)}
.deck .flow{display:flex;gap:.5em;align-items:stretch;margin:.6em 0}.deck .flow>div{flex:1;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:12px;padding:.7em;background:var(--surface-2);font-size:.85em}.deck .flow>i{align-self:center;font-style:normal;color:var(--accent);font-weight:800}
.deck .flow b{display:block}
.deck table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;font-size:.85em}.deck td,.deck th{border:1px solid var(--line);padding:.35em .55em;text-align:left;vertical-align:top}
.deck .quote{font:italic 1.25em/1.4 Georgia,serif;border-left:4px solid var(--accent);padding-left:.8em;margin:.6em 0}
.deck .tag{display:inline-block;font:700 .7em ui-monospace,monospace;padding:.1em .5em;border-radius:6px;background:var(--accent-soft);margin-left:.3em}
.deck.one .slide{display:none;margin:0}.deck.one .slide.current{display:flex}.deck.one>:not(.slide):not(.deck-bar){display:none}
.deck .deck-bar{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:.5em;flex-wrap:wrap;margin:.8em 0 1.2em}.deck .deck-bar button,.deck .deck-pdf{font:inherit;font-size:.9em;font-weight:700;padding:.45em .9em;border-radius:10px;border:1px solid var(--line-2);background:var(--surface);color:var(--ink);cursor:pointer;text-decoration:none}
.deck .deck-bar [data-prev],.deck .deck-bar [data-next]{background:var(--accent);color:var(--accent-ink);border-color:var(--accent);min-width:3em}.deck .deck-bar button:disabled{opacity:.35;cursor:default}
.deck .deck-pos{font:600 .9em ui-monospace,monospace;min-width:4.5em;text-align:center}.deck .deck-gap{flex:1}
.deck.all .deck-bar{position:sticky;bottom:0;background:var(--bg);padding:.5em 0;margin:0}
.deck.full,.deck:fullscreen{position:fixed;inset:0;z-index:1000;background:var(--bg);display:flex;flex-direction:column;align-items:center;justify-content:center;padding:1vh 2vw;font-size:clamp(14px,1.45vw,26px)}
.deck.full .slide.current,.deck:fullscreen .slide.current{width:min(96vw,150vh)}.deck.full .deck-bar,.deck:fullscreen .deck-bar{width:min(96vw,150vh);margin:.6em 0 0}
html.deck-on body{overflow:hidden}
@media (max-width:760px){.deck .slide{aspect-ratio:auto;min-height:70vh;padding:1.1em;overflow:visible}.deck .cols{grid-template-columns:1fr}.deck .flow{flex-direction:column}.deck .flow>i{transform:rotate(90deg)}.deck .slide h1{font-size:2.1em}.deck .slide h2{font-size:1.35em}.deck .deck-gap{display:none}}
@media print{.deck .deck-bar{display:none}}
</style>
<p><a href="../../investors/index.html">For investors</a> · keys ← → · F fullscreen · A all slides. The plain-text version is this page's markdown twin (index.md).</p>
<div class="deck one" data-pdf="../../assets/investors/pitch-deck.pdf">
<section class="slide" aria-label="Cover"><div class="cover"><p class="kick">My Feeds · for investors · Web Summit Lisbon 2026</p><h1>An agentic team that is already working, from the Algarve</h1><p class="big">People with teams of AI agents under written mandates, building and selling in the open. The team is in place; we are looking for investors for it.</p><p class="cap">No numbers and no projections, on purpose: the first six months to a year are for discovering the market by selling. Every claim is sourced on <a href="../../investors/index.html">the investor pages</a>.</p></div></section>
<section class="slide" aria-label="The problem"><h2>Agents can do the work now. Who runs them, and who says what they may do?</h2><div class="cols" style="--n:3"><div class="box"><b>Experts do not scale</b>A teacher, a consultant, an advisor sells hours; the work around each hour (site, bookings, preparation, follow-up) eats them.</div><div class="box"><b>Teams have chats, not teams</b>Anyone can open an AI chat. Few have agents that run on a schedule, with keys, budgets, a record and a person who decides.</div><div class="box"><b>Nobody owns the gap</b>An agent that can read your email can send it. Between what it can do and what it was asked to do is a gap nobody controls.</div></div><p class="cap">Sources: <a href="../../investors/market/index.html">the market</a>.</p></section>
<section class="slide" aria-label="What we do"><h2>We make and run agentic teams, and show the work before we sell it</h2><div class="cols" style="--n:4"><div class="box"><b>For an expert</b>their own agentic team, under rules they set: the first is being made for our first friendly.</div><div class="box"><b>For a team</b>a site, a board, a conductor, a briefing for each person: what this team runs on.</div><div class="box"><b>For an organisation</b>a sourced picture of their world in days, corrected by them: PrompTugal.news.</div><div class="box"><b>For a company running agents</b>a mandate for each agent and the gap made visible: RiskMandate.</div></div><p class="quote">"RiskMandate has to be shown, not explained."</p><p class="cap">The team's strategy, 1 November 2026. <a href="../../investors/positioning/index.html">Positioning</a>.</p></section>
<section class="slide" aria-label="Proof, this week"><h2>Not a mock-up: it is running, in public</h2><ul><li><b>This site</b>: every person, agent, key, policy, decision and release of the Web Summit team, built from a brief on 30 October. <a href="../../team/index.html">The team</a>, <a href="../../agents/index.html">the agents</a>, <a href="../../abp/index.html">the policies</a>.</li><li><b>PrompTugal.news</b>: a newsroom on technology and AI in Portugal, built the same week, every fact with its source.</li><li><b>The first partner who used it</b>: on 6 November Algarve Evolution read the page about itself and asked for a paragraph to be changed. It treated the work as its own.</li><li><b>RiskMandate on ourselves</b>: a published behaviour policy for every agent we run.</li></ul><p class="cap"><a href="../../investors/story/index.html">The story</a>.</p></section>
<section class="slide" aria-label="How we make money"><h2>The code is free. We sell the execution.</h2><div class="cols" style="--n:3"><div class="box"><b>1. Services</b>fixed scope, then changes as asked: a workflow running, a portrait of their world, an event site, a deck. <span class="tag">designed</span></div><div class="box"><b>2. Customised agentic teams</b>set up in the buyer's own accounts with keys, policies and a conductor, then kept running. <span class="tag">first one in progress</span></div><div class="box"><b>3. Packages</b>what sells itself once asked for often enough: a schedule, a summit brief, a vault ticket. <span class="tag">one on sale</span></div></div><p class="quote">"The business model that follows is selling customisation."</p><p class="cap">Dinis Cruz, The value of constraints, 16 October 2026. <a href="../../investors/business-model/index.html">How we make money</a>.</p></section>
<section class="slide" aria-label="Go-to-market"><h2>Show it in the buyer's world, then sell what they ask for</h2><div class="flow"><div><b>Make</b>something about them, from public sources</div><i>›</i><div><b>Send</b>a link, from a person</div><i>›</i><div><b>Listen</b>for "can you change this?"</div><i>›</i><div><b>Wish list</b>their own AI interviews them</div><i>›</i><div><b>Sell</b>what they asked for; a package on the seventh ask</div></div><ul><li><b>Channels</b>: Web Summit (our stand, 12 November), PrompTugal.news, introducers and ecosystems starting in the Algarve, partners who sell with us, writing in the open.</li><li><b>Usage first, then the sale</b>; a person sends every bill and every email.</li></ul><p class="cap"><a href="../../investors/go-to-market/index.html">Go-to-market</a>.</p></section>
<section class="slide" aria-label="Open source"><h2>Open source, because the technology was never the moat</h2><div class="cols" style="--n:2"><div><p class="quote">"The code is open source. The execution is not forkable."</p><ul><li>A fork gets today's position, not the pace.</li><li>What is sold is trust: every line can be read by a buyer or an auditor.</li><li>Anyone can fork, so customers, founders and investors are protected from each other.</li></ul></div><div class="box"><b>The honest weakness</b>The open-source site calls this its most contestable claim. Our answer: keep the pace visible, every release and decision in public, so it can be judged.</div></div><p class="cap">open-source.sgit.ai; The fork next door, 16 October 2026. <a href="../../investors/open-source/index.html">Open source and the moat</a>.</p></section>
<section class="slide" aria-label="The team"><h2>The team is already in place</h2><div class="cols" style="--n:4"><div class="box hi"><b>Dinis Cruz</b>founder and operator: The Cyber Boardroom, MyFeeds.ai, sgit.ai, RiskMandate.ai; CISO; former OWASP Board</div><div class="box"><b>Nimay Parekh</b>business, positioning, investors</div><div class="box"><b>Angelo · Jose Bota</b>engineering, the agents, automation</div><div class="box"><b>Vicky Wang</b>project management</div><div class="box"><b>Silvio Switha</b>ideas, outreach, the Algarve, video</div><div class="box"><b>Indi Gupte · Sarah</b>the message and examples · design</div><div class="box"><b>Daniela</b>the first friendly: the first customised team</div><div class="box"><b>Their agents</b>each person runs their own; the team runs shared ones</div></div><p class="cap"><a href="../../investors/team/index.html">The team</a>.</p></section>
<section class="slide" aria-label="The company"><h2>My Feeds: a technology company in the Algarve</h2><div class="cols" style="--n:2"><div><ul><li><b>MYFEEDS AI, UNIPESSOAL, LDA</b>, a single-member private limited company.</li><li>Seat: <b>Loulé, district of Faro</b>.</li><li>Activity: computer programming and consultancy.</li><li>Incorporated in October 2025; the public directories list no dissolution.</li></ul></div><div class="box"><b>Still to settle, said plainly</b>The official register is to be checked by a person; who owns and manages it, from a register; and which company sells what, between My Feeds and The Cyber Boardroom Limited (UK). Dinis's to set out.</div></div><p class="cap">Racius and eInforma, read 6 November 2026. <a href="../../investors/company/index.html">The company</a>.</p></section>
<section class="slide" aria-label="The investment"><h2>What it is for: time, selling, and scaling the agentic team</h2><ul><li><b>The first six months to a year</b>: discover the market by selling services and customised agentic teams.</li><li><b>Scale the agentic team</b>: more agents, more people running them, the tools that turn one-off work into packages.</li><li><b>Minimal costs by design</b>, so Dinis expects the company to be profitable very fast: his expectation, not a projection.</li><li><b>In rounds</b>, as traction shows; the conversation is how much of the company you want to hold.</li></ul><p class="quote">"The worst possible time to raise money is before you are profitable."</p><p class="cap">Dinis Cruz, 21 September 2026. <a href="../../investors/investment/index.html">The investment</a>.</p></section>
<section class="slide" aria-label="Next"><div class="cover"><p class="kick">Tell us what you think</p><h1>Read it, question it, and tell us what is missing</h1><p class="big">Reply to the person who sent you the link, or let your own AI interview you with <a href="../../investors/feedback/index.html#prompt">our feedback prompt</a>. These pages and this deck change as we get traction; every change is a public commit.</p><p class="cap"><a href="../../investors/index.html">web-summit.sgit.ai/investors</a> · <a href="../../investors/technology-deck/index.html">the technology deck</a> · kept by investors@web-summit.dinis</p></div></section>
</div>
<script src="../../assets/deck.js" defer></script>
